From b089e18cb45ae10b3fd69dda3e136727a7cea6db Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "MD.NAHIAN AHMED" <254077813+nahianahmed3832@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 13:09:21 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(server): WebSocket authentication by first frame for
 browsers

A socket opened without an Authorization header (a browser, which can't set
one) may authenticate with {"t":"auth","token"} as its first frame within
WS_AUTH_TIMEOUT_MS (default 10 s, 100 ms to 60 s). Any other first frame, a
wrong token or silence closes it with 4401 before anything is sent. Header
authentication (the Android app) is unchanged, and the session is still
checked on every frame. Rebased onto API 0.5.0's async frame pipeline.
